# Normalize all text files to LF on checkout for every platform so Windows
# (CRLF) clones cannot corrupt files consumed by Docker, shell, and Next.js.
# A CRLF in docker-compose turns NODE_ENV into "development\r", which disables
# Next.js dev optimizations and can trigger an OOM compilation loop.
# text=auto leaves detected binary files (images, fonts, archives) untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must always be LF.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Every line of the lessons catalog is an independent list item, so a local `git merge` keeps the rows
# both sides added instead of stopping on a conflict. `lessons:check` still fails on a duplicate,
# missing or out-of-order row. GitHub's merge button ignores merge drivers; spec changelogs therefore
# use one file per entry instead (.ai/specs/changelog/README.md). Never set merge=union on a whole
# spec: edits outside the changelog must still conflict.
.ai/lessons.md merge=union
